# Line endings, which decide whether this repository works on a machine that is not mine.
#
# Everything is normalised to LF in the repository. Without this, a clone on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the default of Git for Windows — rewrites text files with CRLF, and
# `backend/mvnw` is a POSIX shell script: run from Git Bash or WSL it fails with a confusing
# `bad interpreter` rather than anything that points at the cause. Windows users get `mvnw.cmd`,
# which is committed too, but the shell script has to survive the checkout either way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that are executed as scripts, spelled out rather than relying on the rule above.
backend/mvnw text eol=lf
frontend/scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: they need CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The raw output of the load test is evidence: kept byte for byte.
backend/measurements/*.txt -text
